fix(compose): land on AlbumPicker review screen w/ Next CTA after picking

Per Dan's screenshots: FB's flow after tapping a video in the picker
is to show a "Next" button which advances to the staging/edit screen.
Earlier I shortcut to step='edit' on file selection — which technically
worked but didn't surface our own "Next" button anywhere, so the user
never saw the visual confirmation step Dan pointed to.

Fix: in SharedPostCreator's handleFiles handoff (the iOS-user-gesture
path) set composeStore.step = 'picker' instead of 'edit'. AlbumPicker
mounts with media already populated, so the auto-fire useEffect is
gated (media.length > 0) and won't re-open the iOS picker. The user
sees the 3-col review grid with their selected items + numbered
selection circles + bottom thumb-strip + sticky blue "Next" button.

Tap Next → AlbumPicker.onNext = () => setStep('edit') → EditPostScreen
with preview tile, description, location, etc. (the staging area).

This matches the FB sequence Dan called out:
  iOS Photos picker → Next button → edit/staging
